{"step_index":2166,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T21:28:15Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 11 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. I previously scanned in 13 leads but after this latest update, all my leads seem to be gone and there are only two remaining.  why did this happen is all data is supposed to be stored locally in an sqlite db?  updating the app itself should not impact what has already been stored.  what if I had call data?  all would have been lost.  this is unacceptable.\n2. that didn't work...still only the two.  so i'll delete those locally and try scanning in again, but i need you to implement world class industry best practices to ENSURE, WITHOUT DOUBT that any data scanned in and notes, calling records, etc. are ABSOLUTELY preserved while beta testing this app.  this type of error CANNOT happen ever again.\n3. do not change the codebase, but explain to me exactly and in detail how the DB is implemented locally.  what initiates the db?  is it in fact sqlite?  give me the details please\n4. would it be better just to keep this a pwa?  i only wanted it mobile os specific to account for the sqlite.  if that's not necessary, would it be advisable and more effective and more cross compatible to focus it as a pwa?\n5. great...step through the code line by line, function by function, module by module and ensure there are no hidden bugs or edge cases, optimize the code and ensure it's operates as a 100% pure PWA\n6. i'm scanning in leads and i just caught a Scan Notice:API gemini-1.5-flash status 404, Not Found.  i think 1.5 flash has been depricated.  you should research and find ALL currently active models and adjust accordingly\n7. now i'm getting 'project not found' on surge\n8. do not change the codebase, but provide a full analysis/assessment of what we've built so far, how well it's suited to its purpose and what, if anything, needs to be added or enhanced to make this a world class dialer solution.\n9. do not change the codebase this turn, but what is the feasibility of being able to automatically pipe scheduled appointments to the users local calendar system...google/apple/outlook calendars?\n10. implement the WORLD-CLASS ENHANCEMENT ROADMAP you recommended in addition to the hybrid scheduling/calendar integration your recommended please\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n# Continuation Summary\n\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Implement World-Class Enhancement Roadmap & Hybrid Calendar Suite:**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"implement the WORLD-CLASS ENHANCEMENT ROADMAP you recommended in addition to the hybrid scheduling/calendar integration your recommended please\"`\n  - *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION** (Hybrid calendar service, objections data, CSV service, planning heatmap screen, campus filtering, and dialer HUD integration are built. Remaining: complete the CSV import/export UI cards in `SettingsScreen.tsx`, test bundle export with `npx expo export -p web`, and deploy to Surge).\n- **Auto-Deploy to Surge Rule (Standing Directive):**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"deploy it to surge please...and do so going forward after every new compile\"`\n  - *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION** (Deploy latest bundle after completing changes to `https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n- **User Directives & Feedback:**\n  - `\"now i'm getting 'project not found' on surge\"` — Resolved by creating `dist/200.html` SPA catch-all fallback.\n  - `\"do not change the codebase, but provide a full analysis/assessment of what we've built so far...\"` — Provided 9.2/10 suitability analysis for ValuTeachers FRS appointment setting.\n  - `\"do not change the codebase this turn, but what is the feasibility of being able to automatically pipe scheduled appointments to the users local calendar system...google/apple/outlook calendars?\"` — Delivered feasibility report (100% feasible via `.ics`, Google Calendar web templates, and Outlook links).\n  - `\"implement the WORLD-CLASS ENHANCEMENT ROADMAP you recommended in addition to the hybrid scheduling/calendar integration your recommended please\"` — Active implementation directive.\n- **Target Company & Business Rules:**\n  - **ValuTeachers** working with Florida educators on FRS, D.R.O.P., and 403(b)/457(b) plans.\n  - Live Surge Domain: `https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n1. **Dynamic Google Gemini API Model Discovery (`src/services/geminiModelService.ts`):**\n   - Built live model discovery querying Google's `GET /v1beta/models` endpoint for the user's API key to prevent 404 deprecation errors, prioritizing high-speed Flash vision models (`gemini-2.5-flash`, `gemini-2.0-flash`, `gemini-3.7-flash`).\n   - Integrated into `src/services/visionService.ts` and `src/services/aiSmsService.ts`.\n2. **Surge SPA Catch-All Fix (`dist/200.html`):**\n   - Created `200.html` mirroring `index.html` to eliminate Surge \"project not found\" errors on sub-routes and page refreshes.\n3. **Hybrid Calendar Service (`src/services/calendarService.ts`):**\n   - Built RFC 5545 `.ics` generator with 15-minute pre-bell alarms (`downloadIcsFile`) for 1-tap Apple Calendar / Outlook opening.\n   - Built direct Google Calendar template web link (`openGoogleCalendar`) and Outlook web link (`openOutlookCalendar`).\n   - Implemented `buildEducatorEvent` pre-filling educator name, school, room number, planning period, and FRS notes.\n4. **Florida Educator Objection Battlecards (`src/data/objections.ts`):**\n   - Created 6 categorized interactive battlecards (`Relationship`, `Time`, `Tenure`, `Pension Context`, `Authority`, `Deflection`) with quick rebuttals, word-for-word scripts, and psychology tips.\n5. **Two-Way CSV / Excel Pipeline Sync (`src/services/csvService.ts`):**\n   - Built `downloadCsv` (Excel UTF-8 BOM formatted) and `parseCsvToLeads` (flexible column header mapper).\n6. **Planning Period Visual Heatmap Screen (`src/screens/PlanningHeatmapScreen.tsx`):**\n   - Created weekly schedule grid across Florida bell schedules (Periods 1–7 + After School), displaying educator appointments, classroom room numbers, and 1-tap dial/calendar action.\n   - Registered in `src/navigation/AppNavigator.tsx`.\n7. **Campus-Clustered Geodialing (`src/db/leadsRepository.ts`, `src/screens/ListsScreen.tsx`):**\n   - Added `getAllSchools()` and `getDialingQueueForSchool(schoolName, listId)` to `LeadsRepository`.\n   - Added horizontal Campus Filter Chip Strip to `ListsScreen.tsx` (`All Campuses`, `DeLand High (4)`, `Pine Ridge (3)`).\n   - Added `Calendar` (Heatmap) and `Download` (Export CSV) buttons to `ListsScreen.tsx` header.\n8. **Dialer HUD Live Battlecards & Calendar Integration (`src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`, `src/screens/LeadDetailScreen.tsx`):**\n   - Added `Scripts` button in HUD header opening the FRS Objections drawer modal.\n   - Injected 1-tap Calendar Sync buttons (Apple, Google, Outlook) into the Appointment Confirmation modal in `DialerHudScreen.tsx` and the Lead Profile card in `LeadDetailScreen.tsx`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Calendar Piping Mechanics:**\n  - On iOS / Safari / Mac: A `text/calendar` Blob with `.ics` extension automatically opens the native Apple Calendar app with the event pre-populated.\n  - On Android / Chrome / Windows: `https://calendar.google.com/calendar/render?action=TEMPLATE` and `https://outlook.live.com/calendar/0/deeplink/compose` open Google Calendar and Outlook in a new tab with zero authentication hurdles.\n- **Expo Web Bundling & Surge Deployment:**\n  - Export command: `npx expo export -p web` (generates `dist/`).\n  - Required post-build steps:\n    1. `Copy-Item -Path \"web\\manifest.json\" -Destination \"dist\\manifest.json\" -Force`\n    2. `Copy-Item -Path \"web\\sw.js\" -Destination \"dist\\sw.js\" -Force`\n    3. Inject PWA tags into `dist/index.html`.\n    4. `Copy-Item -Path \"dist\\index.html\" -Destination \"dist\\200.html\" -Force`\n    5. `npx surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- `src/services/geminiModelService.ts` (NEW): Live Gemini API model discovery and fallback cascade.\n- `src/services/calendarService.ts` (NEW): RFC 5545 `.ics` generator and Google/Outlook URL builders.\n- `src/data/objections.ts` (NEW): Florida educator FRS objection battlecard scripts.\n- `src/services/csvService.ts` (NEW): Excel-compatible CSV pipeline export and bulk roster parser.\n- `src/screens/PlanningHeatmapScreen.tsx` (NEW): Visual bell schedule grid for periods 1–7.\n- `src/navigation/AppNavigator.tsx`: Registered `PlanningHeatmap` screen.\n- `src/db/leadsRepository.ts`: Added `getAllSchools`, `getDialingQueueForSchool`, and `importLeadsBatch`.\n- `src/screens/ListsScreen.tsx`: Added Campus quick-filter chips, Heatmap shortcut, CSV export shortcut, and campus queue routing.\n- `src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`: Added Objection Battlecards modal, HUD Scripts button, and 1-tap Calendar Sync buttons in Appointment Set modal.\n- `src/screens/LeadDetailScreen.tsx`: Added 1-tap Calendar Sync buttons to lead profile card.\n- `src/services/visionService.ts` & `src/services/aiSmsService.ts`: Upgraded to use `GeminiModelService`.\n\n### Viewed Files\n- `src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx`: Lines 340–420 (adding CSV Pipeline Export and Roster Import buttons).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n1. **Finish CSV Pipeline Section in `src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx`:**\n   - In `SettingsScreen.tsx`, add an **\"EXCEL & CSV PIPELINE SYNC\"** card containing:\n     - 📥 **Export Full Pipeline to CSV (Excel)** (calls `CsvService.downloadCsv`)\n     - 📤 **Import School Roster (CSV)** (paste CSV text modal that calls `CsvService.parseCsvToLeads` and `LeadsRepository.importLeadsBatch`)\n2. **Build and Validate Web Bundle:**\n   ```powershell\n   npx expo export -p web\n   ```\n3. **Inject PWA Assets and Deploy to Surge:**\n   ```powershell\n   Copy-Item -Path \"web\\manifest.json\" -Destination \"dist\\manifest.json\" -Force\n   Copy-Item -Path \"web\\sw.js\" -Destination \"dist\\sw.js\" -Force\n   $html = Get-Content \"dist\\index.html\" -Raw\n   $pwaTags = @\"\n       <title>SnapDialer - ValuTeachers Power Dialer</title>\n       <meta name=\"description\" content=\"High-speed field card scanner, power dialer, and FRS scheduling HUD for ValuTeachers.\" />\n       <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#051F14\" />\n       <meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\" content=\"yes\" />\n       <meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\" content=\"black-translucent\" />\n       <meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-title\" content=\"SnapDialer\" />\n       <link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"/manifest.json\" />\n   \"@\n   $html = $html.Replace(\"<title>SnapDialer</title>\", $pwaTags)\n   Set-Content -Path \"dist\\index.html\" -Value $html -Encoding utf8\n   Copy-Item -Path \"dist\\index.html\" -Destination \"dist\\200.html\" -Force\n   npx surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh\n   ```\n4. **Notify User:** Confirm that the World-Class Enhancement Roadmap and Hybrid Calendar Suite are live on `https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`.\n\nYou have the 4 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787239731075]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/.user_uploaded/media_1787239731075.jpg\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15:30:15Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787239731084]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/.user_uploaded/media_1787239731084.jpg\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15:30:15Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb